00:03:51,421 --> 00:03:54,760
fiber optic connections. Then we came in, set up the

57
00:03:54,761 --> 00:03:58,680
headquarters, and we were able to link into those connections to

58
00:03:58,681 --> 00:04:02,520
give the headquarters the connectivity it needed to do the

59
00:04:02,521 --> 00:04:04,780
warfighting. Within months,

60
00:04:04,781 --> 00:04:09,280
CENTCOM was a joint command, part in Tampa and part in Doha.

61
00:04:09,281 --> 00:04:13,280
The two posts worked together to monitor the AOR, manage the

62
00:04:13,281 --> 00:04:17,820
situation in Afghanistan, and conduct the war in Iraq.

63
00:04:17,821 --> 00:04:21,820
We are focused over here on the immediacy of the war effort in

64
00:04:21,821 --> 00:04:25,820
Iraq and Afghanistan. But at the same time, being forward

65
00:04:25,821 --> 00:04:31,820
allows us to go out and engage with all of the 25 countries

66
00:04:31,821 --> 00:04:34,920
that are in this area of responsibility.

67
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:40,320
During the war, this place was a hum of professionalism.

68
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:43,760
Each desk that you see behind me was very busy, gathering

69
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:47,760
information, assessing what it meant within the context of the

70
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:52,880
ongoing battle, and framing decisions for the commander.

71
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:55,680
Having CENTCOM's forward command thousands of miles

72
00:04:55,780 --> 00:05:00,180
away in Qatar and its base back at MacDill, Florida, made for

73
00:05:00,181 --> 00:05:03,020
logistical challenges that only the most sophisticated

74
00:05:03,021 --> 00:05:06,680
communications tools could overcome.

75
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:10,920
Technology today allows us to keep everybody pretty much

76
00:05:10,921 --> 00:05:13,620
informed on what's going on and up to speed.

77
00:05:13,621 --> 00:05:16,420
And that's the real challenge of the split operations.

78
00:05:16,421 --> 00:05:20,140
It's keeping everybody on the same sheet of music.

79
00:05:20,141 --> 00:05:23,140
NavSat Bahrain, this is CENTCOM for a comms check.

80
00:05:23,141 --> 00:05:24,140
How do you read?

81
00:05:24,141 --> 00:05:25,580
CENTCOM, this is NavSat Bahrain.

82
00:05:25,581 --> 00:05:26,780
I have you loud and clear.

83
00:05:26,781 --> 00:05:31,780
Email, satellites, telephones, computer screens, video

